iterations.reply:
I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`. Neither is granted, and no WASI adapter is present. If you want them, the node's `with` clause would have to be widened first (for example with `aap:caps/http-client`).

`wit/world.wit`

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

`src/lib.rs`

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The channel stamps the session identity and delivery status itself;
        // the confirmation is returned as the host produced it.
        response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

